        "id": "s1_slope_half_angle",
        "kind": "equation",
        "label": "Find the slope and write y in half-angle form",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Method",
        "margin_note": "First mark. Three half-angle identities do all the simplifying here: 1 + cos t = 2cos²(t/2), 1 − cos t = 2sin²(t/2) and sin t = 2 sin(t/2)cos(t/2). Convert both y and m before going any further.",
        "lines": [
          {
            "text": "Sol:",
            "style": "heading"
          },
          "(d/dt of t is 1 and d/dt of sin t is cos t;",
          {
            "text": "  1 + cos t = 2cos²(t/2))",
            "style": "indent"
          },
          {
            "text": "x\\ = \\ a\\left(t\\ + \\ \\sin t\\right)\\ \\Rightarrow \\ \\dfrac{dx}{dt}\\ = \\ a\\left(1\\ + \\ \\cos t\\right)\\ = \\ 2a\\cos ^{2}\\left(\\dfrac{t}{2}\\right)",
            "style": "normal",
            "render": "katex"
          },
          "(d/dt of −cos t is sin t;",
          {
            "text": "  sin t = 2 sin(t/2)cos(t/2))",
            "style": "indent"
          },
          {
            "text": "y\\ = \\ a\\left(1\\ - \\ \\cos t\\right)\\ \\Rightarrow \\ \\dfrac{dy}{dt}\\ = \\ a\\sin t\\ = \\ 2a\\sin \\left(\\dfrac{t}{2}\\right)\\cos \\left(\\dfrac{t}{2}\\right)",
            "style": "normal",
            "render": "katex"
          },
          "(for x and y given in terms of t,",
          {
            "text": "  dy/dx = (dy/dt)/(dx/dt))",
            "style": "indent"
          },
          {
            "text": "m\\ = \\ \\dfrac{dy}{dx}\\ = \\ \\dfrac{\\dfrac{dy}{dt}}{\\dfrac{dx}{dt}}",
            "style": "normal",
            "render": "katex"
          },
          {
            "text": "= \\ \\dfrac{2a\\sin \\left(\\dfrac{t}{2}\\right)\\cos \\left(\\dfrac{t}{2}\\right)}{2a\\cos ^{2}\\left(\\dfrac{t}{2}\\right)}",
            "style": "indent",
            "render": "katex"
          },
          {
            "text": "\\left(\\text{cancel}\\ 2a\\ \\text{and}\\ \\text{one}\\ \\cos \\left(\\dfrac{t}{2}\\right);\\ \\dfrac{\\sin }{\\cos } = \\ \\tan \\right)",
            "style": "normal",
            "render": "katex"
          },
          {
            "text": "\\therefore \\ m\\ = \\ \\tan \\left(\\dfrac{t}{2}\\right)",
            "style": "normal",
            "render": "katex"
          },
          {
            "text": "\\left(1\\ - \\ \\cos t\\ = \\ 2\\sin ^{2}\\left(\\dfrac{t}{2}\\right)\\right)",
            "style": "normal",
            "render": "katex"
          },
          {
            "text": "\\text{Also}\\ y\\ = \\ a\\left(1\\ - \\ \\cos t\\right)\\ = \\ 2a\\sin ^{2}\\left(\\dfrac{t}{2}\\right)",
            "style": "normal",
            "render": "katex"
          },
          "Take a > 0 and 0 < t < π, so sin(t/2) > 0, cos(t/2) > 0",
          "and every length below is positive."
